  "title": "Soldiers rescue elderly man, buy him groceries",
  "description": "Florida Army National Guard Staff Sgt. Jason Rivera and Spc. Mark Perez, air and missile defense crewmembers with Bravo Battery, 1st Battalion, 265th Air Defense Artillery Regiment, carry an elderly man through floodwaters to a high-water vehicle after responding to a rescue call at his home in Titusville, Florida, Nov. 23, 2026. After driving through high water to reach the stranded resident, who was running out of food, the Soldiers took him to a local grocery store and personally bought him groceries with their own money during the flooding crisis. (U.S. Army National Guard photo by 1st Lt. Brandon Miles)",
